# The RAM tiers are symlinks out of the repository. Nothing in them is ever
# committed; they hold logs, builds, and scratch that is regenerated on demand.
tmp

# Deprecated temporary scripts are kept for exactly one commit and then removed,
# so they are never ignored -- they are supposed to show up in the record once.

# The repository root ignores anything named "build", meaning build DIRECTORIES in
# other projects. Here "build" is the script that compiles this one -- the single
# file without which a fresh checkout cannot produce a working tree. Un-ignoring
# it is not a preference; a project that cannot be rebuilt from its own record is
# not in the record.
!build

# The documentation site is generated from the Markdown by ./build-docs, and
# nothing in it is ever edited. Committing it would put two hundred and ninety
# files in the record that are a function of files already in the record -- and a
# generated file in a repository is a file somebody eventually edits and then
# wonders why the tool disagrees with it.
docs/HTML/

# Editor and OS litter.
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
